    <h2>What Is Schema Markup?</h2>
    <p>Schema markup (also called structured data) is a standardized code format, usually JSON-LD, that tells search engines exactly what your content means, not just what it says. A page of plain text says "we're open 9 to 5"; schema markup says <em>this is a LocalBusiness, and its openingHours is 09:00-17:00</em> in a format Google can parse with certainty.</p>
    <p>Google uses structured data to understand a page and, for some types, to show richer results, such as business details in a knowledge panel or better title text, images and dates for an article. Two types have lost their search feature: Google says the FAQ rich result is no longer shown in Search (from 7 May 2026) and has removed the How-to rich result, so FAQ and HowTo markup from this generator is valid schema.org code but will not produce those results in Google. Check Google's current documentation before you add markup for a rich result.</p>

    <h2>Which Schema Type Should You Use?</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:16px 0; font-size:0.95rem;">
        <thead>
          <tr style="border-bottom:2px solid currentColor;">
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 8px;">Type</th>
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 8px;">Best for</th>
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 8px;">What Google says today</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.3);"><td style="padding:10px 8px;">FAQPage</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Any page with a genuine Q&amp;A section</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">FAQ rich result no longer shown in Search (from 7 May 2026)</td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.3);"><td style="padding:10px 8px;">HowTo</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Step-by-step instructions</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">How-to rich result removed, no longer shown in results</td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.3);"><td style="padding:10px 8px;">LocalBusiness</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">A physical business location</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">May appear in a knowledge panel with business details such as hours</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Article</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Blog posts and news articles</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Helps Google show better title text, images and dates; no markup is required for Top stories</td></tr>
